note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
note Allen's look: the real sky. Handwritten Omega port of native/kernel/ui/sky_real.c (aienux 4b24df65):
note the gnomonic projection of the catalogue's stars (look-skydata.om) into Nsky, the list of the bright
note ones that twinkle, the twinkle itself (into Nfrm, inside the clip), and the two Magellanic Clouds'
note light and phase maps for the sweeping light. Same integers as the C; tests/look-sky.om compares the
note sky byte for byte with the C oracle.
note Ported: ck_sky_project (skproj), ck_sky_draw_stars (skstars), ck_sky_twinkle (sktwink),
note ck_sky_galaxy_bound/in_view/box/maps (skgbound skginview skgbox skgmaps), and ck_night_init's sky
note construction (skmake, night.c:120-133). Not ported, never reached by the default iMac build (sky_mode 0,
note allen_ui.c:1226): ck_sky_draw_milkyway and its helpers, ck_sky_gmst, ck_sky_zenith, ck_sky_view_at.
note Interface (NIGHT reads these; the names were agreed with LookNight):
note skmake: reads Lg 0..4 (w h k cx cy), runs skinit, clears Nsky w*h, draws the stars into Nsky, fills
note Sktwn/Sktw, then every galaxy's box, offset and maps. Never touches Nfrm or the clip.
note Sktwn: how many stars twinkle (<= 256). Sktw: 8 longs per star i at 8*i: 0 x16, 1 y16 (16ths of a
note pixel), 2 peak (catalogue flux, linear Q16), 3 4 5 col (linear, brightest channel 4096), 6 period
note (ms), 7 phase (ms).
note sktwink i amount: ck_sky_twinkle of star i with amount (1/256 of its flux) into Nfrm, clipped by Lg 5..8.
note Skgbox: x y w h per galaxy (w 0: empty; only galaxies 0 and 1 exist). Skgtint: its sRGB tint.
note Skgper: ms for the sweep to come round. Skgoff: where its maps start in Skglit (light 0..255) and
note Skgpha (phase 0..255), row-major box w*h each. The pools hold every box a 3840-wide screen can need:
note sum of (2a+1)^2 over ck_sky_galaxy_bound = 445^2 + 231^2 = 251386 (Wolfram).
const SKGPOOL ulong 251386
global Sktwn ulong 1
global Sktw long 2048
global Skgbox long 24
global Skgtint uint 6
global Skgper ulong 6
global Skgoff ulong 6
global Skglit uchar SKGPOOL
global Skgpha uchar SKGPOOL
note scratch: Skpx 0 x16 1 y16 (skproj's result), Skgp 0 gx 1 gy (skginview's result);
note Skpk 0 peak 1 2 3 colour, Skclip x y w h, Sktgt 0 Nsky 1 Nfrm (skpoint's arguments);
note Skgw 0 gx 1 gy 2 a 3 b 4 cos 5 sin 6 box x 7 box y 8 a^2 9 b^2 (skgmaps' per-galaxy values for skgpx)
global Skpx long 2
global Skgp long 2
global Skpk ulong 4
global Skclip long 4
global Sktgt ulong 1
global Skgw long 10
note ck_sky_project: where direction (dx dy dz) (Q15) lands on the Lg 0 wide screen whose view centre is
note (Lg 3, Lg 4): Skpx 0 1 in 16ths of a pixel; 0 when behind the camera (more than 88 degrees away).
fn skproj dx long dy long dz long to long
a2 = add mul get Skview 11 dx mul get Skview 12 dy
a2 = add a2 mul get Skview 13 dz
if lt a2 1099511627776
ret 0
end
a2 = shr a2 16
u = add mul get Skview 5 dx mul get Skview 6 dy
u = add u mul get Skview 7 dz
u = div mul u 16384 a2
t = add mul get Skview 8 dx mul get Skview 9 dy
t = add t mul get Skview 10 dz
t = div mul t 16384 a2
s = mul get Lg 0 8
u = div mul u s get Skview 4
t = div mul t s get Skview 4
put Skpx 0 add mul get Lg 3 16 u
put Skpx 1 sub mul get Lg 4 16 t
ret 1
end
note one native pixel of point_add: pixel (x, y) of the target gets weight/256 of the light Skpk
fn skdep x long y long wt ulong to void
i = ulong add mul y get Lg 0 x
c = ulong 0
if eq get Sktgt 0 0
c = ulong get Nsky i
else
c = ulong get Nfrm i
end
out = ulong 0
for k ulong 3
lv = and shr c sub 16 mul 8 k 255
a = mul get Skpk 0 get Skpk add k 1
a = shr mul shr a 13 wt 8
if ne a 0
l = add ulong get Slin lv a
if ge l 32767
l = 4095
else
l = shr l 3
end
lv = shr add ulong get Ssrgb l 8 4
if gt lv 255
lv = 255
end
end
out = or shl out 8 lv
end
c = or and c 4278190080 out
if eq get Sktgt 0 0
put Nsky i uint c
else
put Nfrm i uint c
end
end
note the clip for skpoint: (x, y, w, h) cut to the screen, kept as x0 y0 x1 y1 (ends exclusive) in Skclip
fn skclip x long y long w long h long to void
put Skclip 0 pkmax x 0
put Skclip 1 pkmax y 0
put Skclip 2 pkmin add x w get Lg 0
put Skclip 3 pkmin add y h get Lg 1
end
note point_add: a point source at (x16, y16) deposits the light Skpk on the 2 x 2 native pixels round it,
note inside Skclip (already cut to the screen), into Nsky (Sktgt 0) or Nfrm (Sktgt 1). Weights sum to 256.
fn skpoint x16 long y16 long to void
x0 = shr sub x16 8 4
y0 = shr sub y16 8 4
fx = ulong and sub x16 8 15
fy = ulong and sub y16 8 15
for j ulong 2
y = add y0 long j
if ge y get Skclip 1
if lt y get Skclip 3
for i ulong 2
x = add x0 long i
if ge x get Skclip 0
if lt x get Skclip 2
wt = sub 16 fx
if eq i 1
wt = fx
end
if eq j 1
wt = mul wt fy
else
wt = mul wt sub 16 fy
end
if ne wt 0
skdep x y wt
end
end
end
end
end
end
end
end
note ck_sky_draw_stars for star i: project it, add its light to Nsky, list it to twinkle when V <= 1.0
fn skstar1 i ulong to void
j = mul i 3
if eq skproj get Skstar j get Skstar add j 1 get Skstar add j 2 0
ret
end
x = get Skpx 0
y = get Skpx 1
if lt x -32
ret
end
if lt y -32
ret
end
if gt x add mul get Lg 0 16 32
ret
end
if gt y add mul get Lg 1 16 32
ret
end
bv = get Skbv i
if ge bv 128
bv = 127
end
bv = mul bv 3
put Skpk 0 get Skflux get Skmag i
put Skpk 1 get Skpal bv
put Skpk 2 get Skpal add bv 1
put Skpk 3 get Skpal add bv 2
skpoint x y
if le get Skmag i 59
n = get Sktwn 0
if lt n 256
n = mul n 8
put Sktw n x
put Sktw add n 1 y
put Sktw add n 2 long get Skpk 0
put Sktw add n 3 long get Skpk 1
put Sktw add n 4 long get Skpk 2
put Sktw add n 5 long get Skpk 3
put Sktw add n 6 long add 1200 rem mul i 137 2400
put Sktw add n 7 long rem mul i 919 65536
put Sktwn 0 add get Sktwn 0 1
end
end
end
note ck_sky_draw_stars: every catalogue star in the view into Nsky (clip: the whole screen), the bright
note ones listed in Sktw
fn skstars to void
put Sktwn 0 0
put Sktgt 0 0
skclip 0 0 get Lg 0 get Lg 1
for i ulong SKNST
skstar1 i
end
end
note ck_sky_twinkle: star i of Sktw with amount/256 more of its light, into Nfrm inside the clip Lg 5..8
fn sktwink i ulong amount ulong to void
n = mul i 8
put Skpk 0 shr mul ulong get Sktw add n 2 amount 8
put Skpk 1 ulong get Sktw add n 3
put Skpk 2 ulong get Sktw add n 4
put Skpk 3 ulong get Sktw add n 5
put Sktgt 0 1
skclip get Lg 5 get Lg 6 get Lg 7 get Lg 8
skpoint get Sktw n get Sktw add n 1
end
note ck_sky_galaxy_bound: the side of the largest box galaxy i can need on a w-wide screen (0: no galaxy i)
fn skgbound w long i ulong to long
if ge i SKNGAL
ret 0
end
a = add shr mul get Skgal add mul i 7 3 w 16 4
ret add mul a 2 1
end
note ck_sky_galaxy_in_view: galaxy i's centre pixel into Skgp 0 1; 1 when it is on the Lg 0 x h screen
fn skginview i ulong h long to long
if ge i SKNGAL
ret 0
end
j = mul i 7
if eq skproj get Skgal j get Skgal add j 1 get Skgal add j 2 0
ret 0
end
x = shr add get Skpx 0 8 4
y = shr add get Skpx 1 8 4
put Skgp 0 x
put Skgp 1 y
if lt x 0
ret 0
end
if ge x get Lg 0
ret 0
end
if lt y 0
ret 0
end
if ge y h
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
note ck_sky_galaxy_box: galaxy i's box on the screen into Skgbox (clipped; empty when out of view or none)
fn skgbox i ulong to void
b = mul i 4
put Skgbox b 0
put Skgbox add b 1 0
put Skgbox add b 2 0
put Skgbox add b 3 0
if eq skginview i get Lg 1 0
ret
end
a = add shr mul get Skgal add mul i 7 3 get Lg 0 16 4
x0 = pkmax 0 sub get Skgp 0 a
y0 = pkmax 0 sub get Skgp 1 a
x1 = pkmin sub get Lg 0 1 add get Skgp 0 a
y1 = pkmin sub get Lg 1 1 add get Skgp 1 a
if ge x0 x1
ret
end
if ge y0 y1
ret
end
put Skgbox b x0
put Skgbox add b 1 y0
put Skgbox add b 2 sub x1 x0
put Skgbox add b 3 sub y1 y0
end
note one map pixel (px, py) of the galaxy Skgw describes, at pool offset off: its light and phase
fn skgpx px long py long off ulong to void
px = sub add get Skgw 6 px get Skgw 0
py = sub add get Skgw 7 py get Skgw 1
u = mul px get Skgw 4
u = shr add u mul py get Skgw 5 14
v = mul neg px get Skgw 5
v = shr add v mul py get Skgw 4 14
a = get Skgw 2
note f < 0: no galaxy there (a or b 0, or outside the ellipse u^2 b^2 + v^2 a^2 > a^2 b^2);
note Skgw 8 is a^2, Skgw 9 is b^2
f = long -1
if ne a 0
if ne get Skgw 3 0
f = mul mul u u get Skgw 9
f = add f mul mul v v get Skgw 8
f = sub mul get Skgw 8 get Skgw 9 f
end
end
if lt f 0
put Skglit off 0
put Skgpha off 128
ret
end
note light falls off as (1 - (u/a)^2 - (v/b)^2)^2
f = mul mul u u 65536
f = sub 65536 div f get Skgw 8
v = mul mul v v 65536
f = sub f div v get Skgw 9
if lt f 0
f = 0
end
f = shr mul f f 16
f = shr mul f 255 16
put Skglit off uchar f
f = mul add u a 255
f = div f add mul a 2 1
put Skgpha off uchar f
end
note ck_sky_galaxy_maps: galaxy i's light and phase over its box into Skglit / Skgpha at Skgoff i
fn skgmaps i ulong to void
if ge i SKNGAL
ret
end
b = mul i 4
if eq get Skgbox add b 2 0
ret
end
if eq skginview i 2147483647 0
ret
end
j = mul i 7
put Skgw 0 get Skgp 0
put Skgw 1 get Skgp 1
put Skgw 2 shr mul get Skgal add j 3 get Lg 0 16
put Skgw 3 add shr mul get Skgal add j 4 get Lg 0 16 1
put Skgw 4 pkcos ulong get Skgal add j 5
put Skgw 5 pksin ulong get Skgal add j 5
put Skgw 6 get Skgbox b
put Skgw 7 get Skgbox add b 1
put Skgw 8 mul get Skgw 2 get Skgw 2
put Skgw 9 mul get Skgw 3 get Skgw 3
put Skgtint i uint get Skgal add j 6
put Skgper i add 2400 mul i 400
w = ulong get Skgbox add b 2
h = ulong get Skgbox add b 3
off = get Skgoff i
for py ulong h
for px ulong w
skgpx long px long py off
off = add off 1
end
end
end
note the sky as ck_night_init makes it (night.c:120-133): black, the stars, the galaxies
fn skmake to void
skinit
w = ulong get Lg 0
h = ulong get Lg 1
for y ulong h
r = mul y w
for x ulong w
put Nsky add r x 0
end
end
skstars
off = ulong 0
for i ulong 6
skgbox i
put Skgoff i off
b = mul i 4
off = add off mul ulong get Skgbox add b 2 ulong get Skgbox add b 3
skgmaps i
end
end
